W: Old Molly Hare, What you doing there?
W: Running through the cotton patch as fast as I can tear.
W: 
W: Old Molly Hare, what you doing there?
W: Sitting in my fireplace a-smoking my cigar.
W: 
W: Old Molly Hare, what you doing there?
W: Sitting on a haystack a-shooting at a bear.
W: 
W: Old Molly Hare, what you doing there?
W: Sitting on a butter-plate a-picking out a hair.
W: 
W: Old Molly Hare, your tail’s too short.
W: Yes, doggone it, I can tuck it out of sight.
W: 
W: Dogs say “boo,” and they bark too.
W: I haven’t got the time for to talk to you.
W: 
W: Riding of a goat and leading of a sheep,
W: I won’t be back till the middle of the week.
