X: 974
T: Battle Of New Orleans
C:Jimmy Driftwood
Q: 1/4=100
V:1 
W: [Verse 1]
W: Well, in 18 and 14 we took a little trip
W: Along with Colonel Jackson down the mighty Mississip'
W: We took a little bacon, and we took a little beans
W: And we met the bloody British near the town of New Orleans
W: 
W: [Chorus]
W: We fired our guns, and the British kept a-comin'
W: But there wasn't nigh as many as there was a while ago
W: We fired once more, and they began runnin'
W: On down the Mississippi to the Gulf of Mexico
W: 
W: [Verse 2]
W: Well, I seed Mars Jackson a-walklin' down the street
W: And a-talkin' to a pirate by the name of Jean Lafitte
W: Hе gave Jean a drink that he brung from Tеnnessee
W: And the pirate said he'd help us drive the British in the sea
W: 
W: [Verse 3]
W: The French told Andrew, "You'd better run
W: For Pakenham's a-comin' with a bullet in his gun"
W: Old Hickory said he didn't give a damn
W: He's a-gonna whip the britches off of Colonel Pakenham
W: 
W: [Chorus]
W: We fired our guns and the British kept a-comin'
W: But there wasn't nigh as many as there was a while ago
W: We fired once more, and they began runnin'
W: On down the Mississippi to the Gulf of Mexico
W: 
W: [Instrumental Break]
W: 
W: [Verse 4]
W: Well, we looked down the river, and we seed the British come
W: And there must have been a hundred of 'em beatin' on the drum
W: They stepped so high, and they made their bugles ring
W: While we stood beside our cotton bales, didn't say a thing
W: 
W: [Verse 5]
W: Old Hickory said we'd take 'em by surprise
W: If we didn't fire a musket 'til we looked 'em in the eyes
W: We held our fire 'til we seed their faces well
W: Then we opened up our squirrel guns and really gave 'em hell
W: 
W: [Chorus]
W: We fired our guns and the British kept a-comin'
W: But there wasn't nigh as many as there was a while ago
W: We fired once more, and they began runnin'
W: On down the Mississippi to the Gulf of Mexico
W: 
W: [Post Chorus]
W: Well, they ran through the briars, and they ran through the brambles
W: And they ran through the bushes where a rabbit couldn't go
W: They ran so fast that the hounds couldn't catch 'em
W: On down the Mississippi to the Gulf of Mexico
W: 
W: 
W: [Verse 6]
W: Well, we fired our cannon 'til the barrel melted down
W: So, we grabbed a alligator, and we fought another round
W: We filled his head with Minié balls and powdered his behind
W: And when we touched the powder off, the gator lost his mind
W: 
W: [Verse 7]
W: They lost their pants and their pretty shiny coats
W: And their tails were all a-showin' like a bunch of billy goats
W: They run down the river with their tongues hangin' out
W: And they said they got a lickin' which there wasn't any doubt
W: 
W: [Chorus]
W: We fired our guns and the British kept a-comin'
W: But there wasn't nigh as many as there was a while ago
W: We fired once more, and they began runnin'
W: On down the Mississippi to the Gulf of Mexico
W: 
W: [Verse 8]
W: Well, we marched back to town in our dirty ragged pants
W: And we danced all night with them pretty girls from France
W: We couldn't understand 'em but they had the sweetest charms
W: And we understood 'em better when we got 'em in our arms
W: 
W: [Verse 9]
W: The guide who brung the British from the sea
W: Came a-limpin' into camp just as sick as he could be
W: He said the dyin' words of the Colonel Pakenham
W: Was, "You better quit you're foolin' with your cousin, Uncle Sam"
W: 
W: 
W: [Chorus]
W: Fired our guns, and the British kept a-comin'
W: But there wasn't nigh as many as there was a while ago
W: We fired once more, and they began runnin'
W: On down the Mississippi to the Gulf of Mexico
W: 
W: [Verse 10]
W: Well, we'll march back home but we'll never be content
W: 'Til we make Old Hickory the people's president
W: And every time we think about the bacon and the beans
W: We'll think about the fun we had way down in New Orleans
W: 
W: [Chorus]
W: We fired our guns, and the British kept a-comin'
W: But there wasn't nigh as many as there was a while ago
W: We fired once more, and they began runnin'
W: On down the Mississippi to the Gulf of Mexico
W: 
W: [Post Chorus]
W: Well, they ran through the briars, and they ran through the brambles
W: And they ran through the bushes where a rabbit couldn't go
W: They ran so fast that the hounds couldn't catch 'em
W: On down the Mississippi to the Gulf of Mexico
W: 
W: [Chorus]
W: Fired our guns, and the British kept a-comin'
W: But there wasn't nigh as many as there was a while ago
W: We fired once more, and they began runnin'
W: On down the Mississippi to the Gulf of Mexico
